# Repo-level ignores. backend/ and frontend/ keep their own for the noise
# their toolchains make; this file covers the root and anything that would
# leak a secret from either half.

# Real environment files. `.env.example` is committed on purpose — it names
# every key without valuing any of them (CLAUDE.md).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tool caches that land wherever the command was run from.
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
__pycache__/

# Editors and OS.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Local scratch: logs, coverage, anything a run drops at the root.
*.log
